WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.450
Here are the guide's Step 3 commands,
from Learn's DDoS quickstarts.

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.817
Create one Network Protection plan
in the connectivity subscription,

3
00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:12.000
and link each virtual network
that holds public I Ps.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.324
Or, for I P Protection, enable
it on one Standard public I P.

5
00:00:16.324 --> 00:00:21.775
Turn on diagnostic logs for each
protected public I P, to the workspace.

6
00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:23.213
Then alert on attack.

7
00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:27.837
The metric called Under DDoS attack
or not reads one during mitigation,

8
00:00:27.837 --> 00:00:31.287
and Learn's tutorial alerts
at a maximum of one or more.

9
00:00:31.287 --> 00:00:33.451
One caution from Learn's quickstart:

10
00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:38.282
a virtual network with DDoS protection
can't be moved between resource groups or

11
00:00:38.282 --> 00:00:43.113
subscriptions, and disabling protection
to move it resets the tuned thresholds.

12
00:00:43.113 --> 00:00:46.087
Then hold it with policy
in Step 9: Learn's page,

13
00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:51.071
Secure your Azure DDoS Protection
deployment, names the built-in policies,

14
00:00:51.071 --> 00:00:55.412
one that protects virtual networks
with a Modify or Audit effect,

15
00:00:55.412 --> 00:00:58.440
and one that requires
the DDoS resource logs.
